auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  KanaSanté API collection. Every /v1 request inherits the bearer token set by the
  sign-in requests in auth/ (better-auth returns it in the `set-auth-token` response
  header — no manual copying). Seed the demo accounts first: `bun run db:seed` with
  the DEMO_* vars from .env.local.example, then run auth/ or flows/demo.

  To verify a working end-to-end API without filling variables by hand, select the
  local environment and run the entire flows/demo folder. Its requests capture and
  pass tokens and resource IDs to later steps. The blank path parameters under
  v1/ are intentional: those files are the exhaustive endpoint catalog and need a
  concrete resource ID when run individually.

  bruno/v1/** is generated from the OpenAPI spec by `bun run bruno:scaffold` and
  enforced by test/api/bruno-coverage.api.test.ts: every documented operation must
  have a request file here, and every request file must match a documented operation.
}
